  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Dog Attitude is a family boarding kennel for dogs and cats on chemin de l'Oratoire in Mougins, run by Sandrine Raclin according to several converging directories. Unlike the home-based dog sitters listed elsewhere on the site, this is a professional facility with dedicated premises: individual heated kennels, each with an outdoor run of about 30 sqm, under video surveillance, on a 3-hectare wooded site with direct access to the Mougins departmental park (fenced, secure play areas of 300 to 500 sqm in addition to the kennels). The boarding kennel also offers breeding, training and grooming.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Two packages are advertised: a studio stay with terrace, between €17 and €21 per animal, or an outdoor-park stay with a compatible companion, between €20 and €24 a night. Online reviews mention a professional, attentive welcome, with a team committed to the animals' wellbeing. <strong>As with any boarding kennel</strong>, it's best to reconfirm current prices and availability directly by phone, and if possible visit the facilities before a first booking, especially for a multi-day stay.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if you're torn between a kennel with runs and home boarding, consider your dog's sociability and temperament — individual kennels with runs suit dogs that need calm, while boarding at a private individual's home may suit a dog used to family life better.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Mougins sits between Cannes and Grasse, a hilltop village known for its old town and its food scene, right next to Mouans-Sartoux and the Parc de la Valmasque.</p>
